{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c571","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0835a-066b-7002-8c2a-c1f520e9ef11"},"sequence":275,"recorded_at":1780531400000545,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5e62c3f8-6d84-4b89-ab73-2ad027ebf2e5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5e62c3f8-6d84-4b89-ab73-2ad027ebf2e5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5e62c3f8-6d84-4b89-ab73-2ad027ebf2e5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"008d96f8-dbab-4404-b0ec-8443d636a5fb"},"task_id":"008d96f8-dbab-4404-b0ec-8443d636a5fb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"008d96f8-dbab-4404-b0ec-8443d636a5fb","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2439 line(s) above)\n2440|framing (`DecodeQuery`, `CheckCursorReuse`). Six executable\n2441|acceptance cases (`directory-node-bootstrap`,\n2442|`directory-node-manifest`, `directory-node-probe`,\n2443|`directory-node-scan`, `directory-node-query`,\n2444|`directory-node-idempotency`) bind those entry points to their\n2445|named positive and refusal tests, and an AST-derived refusal-arm\n2446|inventory (`census_test.go`) requires every production refusal arm\n2447|— literal, fault-detail conduit, and branch-prefix expression\n2448|shapes — to resolve to a named asserting test in both directions,\n2449|with two recorded defensive arms that no public input can fire.\n2450|The Section 7.9 clause-level binding stays `unevidenced` (catalog\n2451|`ForRelease` only): no clause of 7.9 is enumerated against an\n2452|acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim\n2453|about the obligations it carries. The framed subset is exactly\n2454|manifest, probe, and scan plus the Directory Query contract; the\n2455|remaining eight registry operations carry nested content owned by\n2456|the sibling leaves and are pinned as unframed by\n2457|`TestFramedSubsetIsExact`, not silently absent.\n2458|\n2459|Successful output reports ownership inventory counts and the measured coverage\n2460|ratio only. The gate does not mutate repository or product state, add an `ax`\n2461|command or `doctor` result, or claim that any catalog capability is available,\n2462|enabled, or supported.\n2463|\n2464|## Managed Skills\n2465|\n2466|`Skillfile.json` targets the Curator-standard `claude_code` and `codex_cli`\n2467|agent adapters and pins this project-local skill to an exact revision:\n2468|\n2469|| Skill | Revision |\n2470|| --- | --- |\n2471|| `relux-works/skill-go-testing-tools` | `90c1515239eed9321068f3bafbeb5d0a0c2aa26a` |\n2472|\n2473|Project management is intentionally global. The repository does not declare or\n2474|install `project-management`; development uses the globally installed skill\n2475|and `task-board` CLI.\n2476|\n2477|Repository development routing in `task-board.config.json` admits only Codex\n2478|`gpt-6-astra` with `medium` or `high` reasoning for all new spawns, including\n2479|producers and reviewers. Mechanical, documentation, and operations workloads\n2480|recommend medium first; all other workloads, including review, recommend high\n2481|then medium. Every recommendation uses Astra. Existing runs and their work are\n2482|preserved. Retained Claude and Muse ceiling definitions are inactive under\n2483|exclusive Codex admission; Claude, Muse, and Fable are not active spawn routes.\n2484|\n2485|Inspect effective admission and recommendations before spawning:\n2486|\n2487|```bash\n2488|task-board q 'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=developer, agent=codex, workload_class=mechanical)'\n2489|task-board q 'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=reviewer, agent=codex, workload_class=review)'\n2490|```\n2491|\n2492|Preflight prints JSON to stdout; save task validation evidence under\n2493|`.temp/<TASK-ID>/` and attach it to the owning board item.\n2494|\n2495|Curator owns `.agents/`, `.claude/skills/`, and `.codex/skills/`. Do not edit\n2496|their generated contents directly; change `Skillfile.json` and rerun Curator.\n2497|\n2498|## Tools and Outputs\n2499|\n2500|| Tool | Purpose | Command or entry point | Outputs |\n2501|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n2502|| Curator | Pin, install, and validate project skills | `curator install`; `curator status --check` | `.agents/`, `.claude/skills/`, `.codex/skills/` |\n2503|| `task-board` | Track scope, lifecycle, checklists, evidence, dependency waves, and the critical path through the global `project-management` installation | `task-board q 'plan()'`; `task-board q 'plan(TASK-260830-55kcni, mode=related)'`; `task-board plan --save` | `.task-board/`; `.planning/`; task outcome resources |\n2504|| Go toolchain | Verify global and assigned-scope specification ownership, validate versioned Configuration readers/current writer, validate owner-local storage, immutable installs, and SQLite rebuild/recovery, validate and fuzz common wire scalars, canonical identities, core records, Session Events, and Observation Events, validate the Structured Error registry, its static containing-contract bindings, and its detail redaction, validate the CLI Result envelopes, command bodies, common flags, rendering boundary, and exit-status mapping, classify one completed `ax --json` invocation from stdout and its exit status through the machine reader and replay the frozen historical envelope corpora, generate and check the typed catalogs, build, test, and measure the Go implementation | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck`; `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2` (every other assigned section is refused with its measured coverage ratio); `go test ./internal/config -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/localstore -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/scalar -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/scalar -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzScalarProductionEntries$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/axerror -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/cliresult -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObservationEventRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go generate ./internal/catalog`; `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.5.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; `go test ./... -v`; `go test ./... -cover`; `go build ./...` | Read-only traceability report; owner-only roots, immutable blob/quarantine data, and `<state>/index.sqlite` plus recovery evidence only when storage entries are called; `internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go`; Go build/fuzz cache; test output captured under `.temp/<TASK-ID>/` when needed |\n2505|| `github.com/gowebpki/jcs` | RFC 8785 byte transformation after repository-owned strict I-JSON validation | Imported by `internal/canonicaljson.Canonicalize` at pinned module version `v1.0.1` | Canonical UTF-8 JSON bytes in memory; no durable output |\n2506|| `github.com/pelletier/go-toml/v2` | Parse and emit TOML while the repository-owned Configuration layer enforces exact versioned closed schemas | Imported by `internal/config.Decode`, `internal/config.EncodeCurrent`, and explicit `internal/config.Migrate` at pinned module version `v2.4.3` | Validated Configuration values/TOML bytes in memory; explicit migration writes a same-directory replacement plus an owner-only versioned backup |\n2507|| `modernc.org/sqlite` | Provide the pure-Go SQLite driver for the local derived index without a CGO platform dependency | Imported by `internal/localstore.OpenProjection` at pinned module version `v1.57.0` | `<state>/index.sqlite`, its owner-only lock and WAL/SHM/journal sidecars, and `<state>/index-recovery/<uuid>/` corruption evidence |\n2508|| `golang.org/x/sys` | Invoke OS-native no-replace rename primitives so concurrent processes cannot overwrite an immutable digest path | Imported by `internal/localstore.atomicRenameNoReplace` at pinned module version `v0.47.0` | Same-filesystem atomic rename only; no standalone artifact |\n2509|| GitHub Actions | Enforce traceability, generated-output, test, vet, and build gates on pull requests and `main` | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | GitHub-hosted CI check results |\n2510|| Git | Branch, diff, and create signed commits/tags | `git status`; `git diff --check`; `git commit -S`; `git tag -s` | Git objects and refs under `.git/` |\n2511|| GitHub CLI | Inspect and open pull requests after bootstrap | `gh pr create`; `gh pr checks` | Pull requests and checks on GitHub |\n2512|\n2513|Temporary validation logs and worktrees belong under `.temp/<TASK-ID>/` and\n2514|must not be committed. Diagrams, when implementation work introduces them,\n2515|belong under `diagrams/`.\n2516|\n2517|Configuration loading, migration, and downgrade assessment use the existing Go\n2518|toolchain entry in the tools table. Focused outputs are Go test/coverage results\n2519|and the read-only traceability report; migration writes only when its explicit\n2520|production entry is called, and task-scoped captured logs belong under\n2521|`.temp/<TASK-ID>/`.\n2522|\n2523|## Contribution Baseline\n2524|\n2525|All non-bootstrap changes are delivered automatically through pull requests as\n2526|author-signed commits, then landed by fast-forwarding the exact reviewed head\n2527|into `main`. Before creating a branch or task-scoped worktree, fetch\n2528|`origin/main`, fast-forward local `main`, and verify the refs are equal. Track\n2529|the work in `task-board`, use the managed `go-testing-tools` skill for Go\n2530|changes, use the global `project-management` skill for orchestration, run\n2531|relevant validation, and attach task-scoped evidence before review. See\n2532|[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the full contract."}}}
